# `Map` — key-to-value lookup

```java
Map<String, Integer> ages = new HashMap<>();
ages.put("Ada", 36);
ages.put("Ada", 37);              // same key → replaces
ages.get("Ada");                  // 37
ages.get("nobody");               // null
ages.getOrDefault("nobody", 0);   // 0 — safer read
```

Keys form a `Set` (unique). Missing `get` → `null`.

## Methods that prevent bugs

```java
counts.merge(word, 1, Integer::sum);                      // tally
groups.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(x);  // group
ages.putIfAbsent("Ada", 99);
```

Replace the `containsKey … else …` dance.

## Iterate a view

```java
for (var e : ages.entrySet())            // both key & value, one pass
    ... e.getKey() ... e.getValue();
```

`keySet()` · `values()` · `forEach((k,v) -> …)`

## Impls & the key contract

`HashMap` (default, no order) · `LinkedHashMap` (insertion) · `TreeMap` (sorted).
**Keys need correct `equals`/`hashCode`** — use **immutable** keys.
